  "result": "I wrote the 30-minute lesson on context and memory (O3), and a five-item quiz with its key. I haven't opened the lesson in a browser or counted its words. By my estimate it's about 3,400 words, which fits the length check for 30 minutes.\n\n**What the lesson covers**\n- **Context window:** what the model sees on each call.\n- **Between steps:** the whole message history is resent on every call. A worked example of one makerspace request shows the cost adding up: 14,080 input tokens in total, even though the final context is only about 5,400. The token sizes are invented for the example.\n- **Between sessions:** the model keeps nothing, so any memory has to be saved outside it and put back into the context.\n- **Notes as memory:** a worked example of saving and reloading a student's training status.\n- **Retrieval:** how to find the right page in a long manual.\n- **Where each piece goes:** a worked example sorting information into the system prompt, notes, retrieval, or a live tool call.\n- **Practice and sources:** three practice questions with instant feedback, a faded \"your turn\" cost exercise, and links to the sources (Anthropic's context-engineering post, the Claude context-window and memory-tool docs, Contextual Retrieval, and \"Lost in the Middle\").\n\n**Where the files are**\n- Lesson: `lessons/0001-context-and-memory-in-an-agent.html`\n- Quiz and key: `quizzes/0002.json` and `keys/0002.json` (it's number 0002 because quiz 0001 already exists)\n- Also written: `cheatsheets/0001-context-and-memory.html`, `RESOURCES.md`, and a line in `NOTES.md`\n\nThe quiz is ready when you are. You can ask me anything about the lesson.\n\nOne thing to check: quiz 0001 is still ungraded, with two submissions, `s1` and `s2`. Do you want me to grade those next?",
